# Deploy Indexer to GCE

## Target VM
- Host: `35.188.116.99`
- SSH: `ssh -i ~/.ssh/gcp-gce-01 gcp-vm-monopoly@35.188.116.99`
- Deploy path: `/opt/x402-xrpl`
- Service: `x402-indexer` (systemd)

## Database
- Private IP: `10.77.97.16:5432`
- Database: `x402_xrpl`
- User: `postgres`
- Password: `>GX-Z8}rsarm0$jx`

## Deploy Steps

1. SSH into VM and pull latest code:
```bash
ssh -i ~/.ssh/gcp-gce-01 gcp-vm-monopoly@35.188.116.99
cd /opt/x402-xrpl && git pull origin main
```

2. Install deps, generate Prisma, build:
```bash
pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
pnpm db:generate
pnpm --filter @x402-xrpl/indexer build
```

3. Restart service:
```bash
sudo systemctl restart x402-indexer
```

4. Check logs:
```bash
sudo journalctl -u x402-indexer -f --no-pager
```

## Key Files on VM
- Env: `/opt/x402-xrpl/apps/indexer/.env`
- JS entry: `packages/database/index.js` (compiled JS, not .ts)
- Service: `/etc/systemd/system/x402-indexer.service`
- DB `main` field in `packages/database/package.json` is `index.js` on VM

## Important Notes
- The database package uses `index.js` (not `index.ts`) on the VM because Node.js can't run TypeScript directly. Don't overwrite this with git pull.
- After `git pull`, if `packages/database/package.json` reverts `main` to `index.ts`, change it back to `index.js`.
- XRPL mainnet WebSocket: `wss://s1.ripple.com:51233`
- Health check: `curl http://localhost:4000/health`
